\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Complira Knowledge Graph \'97 LLM Enrichment Agent Layer\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 Why LLMs Are Essential (Not Optional) for This Graph\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The deterministic ingestion pipeline gets you ~70% of the graph's value. The remaining ~30% \'97 which is where the defensible moat lives \'97 requires intelligence that no API or parser can provide:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 NVD has ~25,000 CVEs with no CWE mapping.
\f1\b0  No API gives you this. An LLM reading the CVE description can classify them.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 ~50,000 packages in deps.dev have no CPE match in NVD.
\f1\b0  Without PURL
\f2 \uc0\u8596 
\f1 CPE resolution, those packages are invisible to the vulnerability graph. An LLM can reason about vendor/product naming.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 CWE
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0 CRA requirement mappings don't exist anywhere.
\f1\b0  The EU published CRA text. MITRE published CWEs. Nobody published the crosswalk. An LLM with both documents can create it.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 VEX justifications require reasoning
\f1\b0  about exploit conditions, binary hardening, network reachability, and compensating controls \'97 exactly what LLMs excel at.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \strokec2 Without the LLM layer, you have a data warehouse. With it, you have an intelligence platform.
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

