\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 L5: CVE Description Entity Extractor\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Problem:
\f1\b0  NVD CVE descriptions contain rich structured information buried in free text: affected version ranges, component names, attack vectors, privilege requirements, and impact descriptions. The NVD API provides SOME of this in structured fields, but ~40% of CVEs have incomplete structured data.\

\f0\b Example:
\f1\b0  "A heap-based buffer overflow in libpng before 1.6.44 allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary code via a crafted PNG file."\

\f0\b Extractable entities:
\f1\b0  component=libpng, version_fixed=1.6.44, attack_vector=remote, cwe_implied=CWE-122 (heap overflow), impact=code_execution, trigger=crafted_PNG_file\

\f0\b Model:
\f1\b0  Claude Haiku 4.5 (fast extraction task)\

\f0\b Prompt:
