\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 Quality Assurance & Hallucination Prevention\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Function Calling for Structured Output\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 All LLM agents use JSON-mode structured output (via system prompt instructions + Pydantic validation). The LLM never generates free-form text that goes directly into the graph \'97 every output is parsed, validated, and type-checked.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Evidence Grounding (Anti-Hallucination)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The VEX synthesizer (L3) and Threat Model Generator (L9) are the highest-risk agents for hallucination. They're constrained by:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls18\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Input-only citation rule
\f1\b0 : The prompt explicitly states "only cite evidence provided in the input." The Pydantic output model requires 
\f5\fs26 evidence_citations
\f1\fs24  that reference specific input fields.\
\ls18\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Post-generation validation
\f1\b0 : After LLM output, a deterministic validator checks that every 
\f5\fs26 evidence_citation
\f1\fs24  references data actually present in the input context. Any ungrounded citation triggers rejection.\
\ls18\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Cross-reference check
\f1\b0 : For VEX "not_affected" justifications, verify that the claimed mitigation (e.g., "ASLR enabled") actually appears in the 
\f5\fs26 binary_hardening_profiles
\f1\fs24  data for that component.\
\ls18\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Confidence calibration
\f1\b0 : Track accuracy over time. If an agent's auto-applied outputs are frequently overridden by human review, lower the auto-apply threshold.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 Human Review Queue\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Outputs below the auto-apply threshold but above the discard threshold enter a review queue stored in ArangoDB:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f5\fs26 \cf0 FOR e IN llm_enrichments\
    FILTER e.validated == false AND e.human_reviewed == false\
    FILTER e.confidence >= 0.5\
    SORT e.timestamp DESC\
    RETURN \{agent: e.agent, confidence: e.confidence, output: e.output\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 A simple web UI (or even an ArangoDB Foxx microservice) can present these for one-click approve/reject, updating the 
\f5\fs26 human_reviewed
\f1\fs24  and 
\f5\fs26 review_decision
\f1\fs24  fields and applying the enrichment to the graph if approved.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
